      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An 88-year-old man was admitted to the intensive care unit after the ingestion of 150 mg of dehydrocodeine. The ECG showed severe brodycardia and he was diagnosed as sick sinus syndrome. The recovering of sinus node function took 5 days after the ingestion. The complication observed suggests that transient hypoxia induced by ingestion of high dose DHC had affected sinus node."},
